## 4. Symptom → fix

| Symptom | Fix |
|---|---|
| `winetricks dotnet48` fails, or `wpfgfx_v0400.dll` missing afterwards | `cabextract` not installed (1.1) |
| `^[[200~` or trailing `~` in commands; `ls: command not found` | Bracketed-paste corruption — run from a file (1.3) |
| `[sudo] password for root:` then nothing | Account lacks sudo — do Section 1 from an admin account |
| `0xc06d007e`, `ieframe.dll` OLE errors, generic Wine "Program Error" | Native .NET missing from that prefix (1.1, 3.3) |
| `FileNotFoundException at MS.Internal.NativeWPFDLLLoader.LoadCommonDLLsAndDwrite()` | Same — `winetricks -f corefonts dotnet48` (3.3) |
| Mono or `wpfgfx_cor3.dll` errors despite "already installed" | winetricks false positive — force reinstall with `-f` (3.3) |
| Paths collapse to `/drive_c/...` | `WINEPREFIX` empty in this shell — `source ~/.hdt-env` (3.4) |
| `unimplemented function msdelta.dll.ApplyDeltaW, aborting` | `winetricks msdelta` on the Steam prefix (3.5) |
| `exit code 80131506` **with** the msdelta message | Same as above (3.5) |
| `exit code 80131506` from the installer, run against the Steam prefix | Unsolved — use the disposable prefix (2, 8.2) |
| `exit code 80131506` from the app exe, no `packages/` folder present | Unsolved — install properly via Part A (8.1) |
| `wine client error:0: version mismatch` | Wrong Wine build for that prefix (3.1) |
| `System.IO.DirectoryNotFoundException` | Wrong username in path — `steamuser` vs `$USER` (3.2) |
| `getcwd(): No such file or directory` | `cd` into a stable directory before launching Wine (3.7) |
| `pgrep -f Hearthstone.exe` returns nothing | Battle.net is running but the game isn't — press Play (1.4) |
| Battle.net and HDT won't run together | Stop launching via Lutris/Bottles (3.6) |
| Overlay needs double-clicks | Update HDT to ≥ v1.56.3 (3.7) |
| Login does nothing, no browser opens | Known, two causes — use token transfer (6) |

